  "observations": [
    "Unchanged committed adapters fail the first native URL image comparison. The retained actual/expected images have nonempty differences, with failed wait/runner logs. Their document-only assertion records are not passing qualification.",
    "The new type classifiers route URL and telephone into the existing native text editor. Both final fixtures pass 55 checks/23 complete native images, including existing plain/password/Unicode text behavior.",
    "Real-seat Ctrl+A uses native Emacs beginning rather than browser select-all. Native text insertion emits one original trusted beforeinput/input pair; cancellation retains the canonical value and full native image.",
    "Alt+C from a URL input and Alt+V into a telephone input use original trusted copy/paste/beforeinput/input with insertFromPaste. Original URL validity, telephone pattern validity and script URL sanitization remain intact.",
    "Read-only and disabled fields, script updates, text/URL/telephone type transitions and beforeinput retirement/native release pass. Browser parent processes keep their original UI components.",
    "Both independently rebuilt adapter reproductions are byte-identical to their tested candidates. All 20 measured production files, the current shared UI loader/provider/shim and preceding adapters remain unchanged. Descendant renderers retain Seccomp=2/NoNewPrivs=1 and no candidate mappings remain after shutdown."
  ],
  "open": [
    "Search fields, email/number/date/time/file/color and other specialized webpage controls, richer editing, placeholder/style semantics, IME/accessibility and wider scaling/layout/lifecycle contracts.",
    "Other browser builds and derivatives, complete detached menus/native shortcuts and installed deployment, followed by GTK/Qt/KDE using the same shared native UI library.",
    "Browser toolbar, address bar and tabs keep their original components; optional future changes belong to app-specific patches."
  ]
